    "rating": 2.1,
    "reference": "ChIJHU0kx-E3yUwRlQpk3ijA4F0",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "TM JD",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/113743345027214725797/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU7I3tKw7Db1YHYPA3u0upDtjPIvF9LUGrK4uIVQw4adc1y0x4=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "7 months ago",
        "text": "So I went to contest for the first time in my life a stop sign ticket, which was unlawfully given to me by a female police officer who hated that I was speaking English to her. While waiting before everyone could enter the hall I talked to a woman, who said it was her 3rd time contesting stop sign ticket!! She had absolutely no regret for not stopping at the sign and said she knew what to say and because she spoke French no ticket would be given to her. I could not believe my ears. Out of at least 10 people present in court contesting various tickets not a single French speaking person was found guilty. Every non white person and majority of the  English speaking contestant were found guilty. I’m a white person, I speak 3 languages, it was the first time I saw white judge and all his « friends » in court treating immigrants so badly. It’s such a shame!  I have sent a complaint to address discrimination issues in this court and of course my concerns were dismissed.",
        "time": 1752178789,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "gurbani K.",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118212013851420234365/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJJ3iTY_lcPgQHph9Rpe3-F-DJwRaSbGdJOmMM76XeyO_xJ6Q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "10 months ago",
        "text": "At what time exactly you guyz are open? Your cops are everywhere printing tickets for no reason.. discriminating people just coz they  have better cars. And a normal person can’t even go there to put their stupid tickets on fight. Because THE MUNCIPAL  IS CLOSED. You guyz know normally people work bw 8:30 to 4:30 and now you guyz are closed afternoon on Friday. We’re paying taxes more than what we earn and get no return at the end of the year still  we in fact owe to the government. Then why can’t they afford to have 1 employee to work for the  public atleast. If you can pay cops to keep an eye on people with color and with cool cars in every corner and every street day and night thn afford to have one employee at the muncipal office too.",
        "time": 1743791035,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Simon Robillard",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/115855672097310194529/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJfDOXhrebXj1TMojGbjk4fmBMyV2So7Tuitph6ofJLSBNrXw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "2 years ago",
        "text": "Terrible terrible terrible horrific service.\nI did all due diligences on my end, took great lengths to ensure every details was accounted for in describing the ticket duplication error that occured. I talked directly to the prosecutor to have a delay of court, to which he agreed. I then never received communication of the later date and I am forced to pay up close to 6 times the amount of the ticket which was doublecharged (technical error) in the first place. Completely crazy, out of control , improper conduct of justice as well as plain disservice to someone that was ready to pay the original ticket (but was simply contesting its duplication due to technical error). They admitted their error and still said I had no recourse except paying the x6 amount or asking for a retraction of judgement for an additional 50$ on top that can of course be denied by the judge. I am absolutely baffled that something that can add up quite heavily for a citizen isn't managed in a proper manner. The other reviews are absolutely correct. Why am I not capable of having a clear system of communication with them (such as email), that would have avoided all of this.",
        "time": 1678482000,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Dan Wolf",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110910836710870372906/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ_ZWANX1Nsutgiqm6rCB1E4OO_uQ2NbcYXXSG2s-D_ERgF-A=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "4 years ago",
        "text": "Terrible! I agree with other reviewer that this is a Place of INjustice. I'd say even a local \"mafia\" place: the judge talks to the prosecutor beforehand and makes up his mind in advance.\nI had a crazy case where the police agent clearly went on hunt to fulfill her ticket quota and gave me a ticket for non-traffic violation. The judge simply said that I \"did not convince\" him that I was right.\nSo, if the prosecutor offers you a very mediocre settlement, you'd better take it, because there is no justice in this court and you are doomed to lose.\nLast thing: the hearings are held in French ONLY. You will be given an interpreter, but they speak so fast that he cannot really follow them. The judge does understand English, but he will respond to you in French.",
        "time": 1616435570,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "john wilson",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/106937302899130253903/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXTe4PnT7eEBYbWGTbBogeddGUK8-t8PYyLH5k3zizkAS4zYjw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "3 years ago",
        "text": "Great place!\nProfessional staff,\nI got an interpreter eng/fr free,\nHe was very good and curtious,\nProsecutor's offer was acceptable,\nI was in and out in 15 minutes.\nSour comments mostly come from peeps ,\nWho most likely lost their case... :-/",
        "time": 1649970119,
        "translated": false
      }
    ],
